    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog hinges on navigating a difficult encounter with Emmet Sheehan, who is suppressing the ceilings of several core starters. Despite the tough matchup, **Will Smith** remains our anchor with a 64.10 score; he is the most reliable play in the lineup, benefiting from a prime #2 hole and solid xwOBA metrics that provide a high floor even against quality arms. **Masyn Winn** follows close behind at 60.25, capitalizing on an advantageous park factor (+10%) and favorable SP skills (4.35 xERA) that allow him to maintain elite value despite the constraints of his slot. **Brendan Donovan** also projects as a strong play at 59.46, buoyed primarily by his leadoff position and a distinct platoon advantage against Burrows, which elevates his scoring potential despite the marginal park adjustments.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots remains cautious, as evidenced by the performance of our lower-tier starters. **Gavin Sheets** (41.47) and **Matt Chapman** (43.58) are teetering near our 40.0 baseline, largely suppressed by the strength of opposing pitching; **Bryson Stott** (44.98) faces a particularly difficult hurdle against Ranger Suarez, where a -13% platoon penalty and a -4% drain due to limited SB opportunities kept his score depressed. **Drew Gilbert** was the most compelling candidate to challenge for a start, finishing just shy of the floor at 36.02. His exclusion was ultimately dictated by his projected #8 spot in the order and the heavy penalty associated with facing Sheehan, which outweighed his base projection. Owners should note that our lineup relies heavily on pending confirmations; if **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, or **Jung Hoo Lee** are pushed down in their respective orders, their scores will require immediate re-evaluation against our bench depth.",
